'' A CAST WHOSE TYPE IS THE CONSTRUCTOR'S PARAMETER'S EXACTLY DOES NOT BUILD THE OBJECT, as in
'' fbc-modern: 'operator cast( ) as long' into 'constructor( byval k as long )' is refused in
'' every context -- and so is any pointer pair but an identical typed pointer, 'any ptr'
'' included. tiko took every such chain (UserConvCost_'s two-level arm and PickStructor, both
'' through StructorCastCost, src/symbols/structpick.bas), and the operator form, refused for a
'' string cast already, was not a diagnostic at all: TKO0994. The author's call, 2026-10-10:
'' match fbc. See cast-ctor-chain-accepted.test for the neighbours fbc takes.
''
'' QL also casts to double -- a converting pair on its own -- and still the identical cast is
'' the one fbc picks for the long parameter, and refuses.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 with -maxerr inf over the source, 2026-10-10: errors on exactly
'' lines 36-41 and 44, and no others --
''
''     36-37  error 58   an argument to 'byref' and 'byval as E'
''     38     error 20   an operand of 'operator <>( E, E )'          (TKO0820 here)
''     39     error 24   an initialiser, 'dim as E e1 = x'             (TKO0738)
''     40     error 99   'E( x )'                                      (TKO0632)
''     41     error 58   'long ptr' into a constructor taking 'any ptr'
''     44     error 181  'return z' from a function returning E        (TKO0738)
